--- !u!114 &7435934264335208615
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 7435934264335208614}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: dff0893e3b676c741954ac055f09ffdd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _loadingSpeed: 0.5
  _loadingUI: {fileID: 7435934263554107355}
  _waitTime: 0.5
  _tooltipText: {fileID: 7435934263771603389}
  _progressFillImage: {fileID: 4023819014139143494}
  _progressPercentText: {fileID: 1536894166767289766}
  _statusText: {fileID: 7009117140845744989}
  _toolTips:
  - New players can type !create to make a character.
  - Need to switch your role? Type !role followed by the role you want to switch
    to.
  - Going AFK for a while? Hit the Esc key and turn on Idle Mode to give full control
    to your Twitch chat.
  - 'Certain buildings will unlock additional role slots for certain roles. '
  - Loggers will collect Wood. If you need more Loggers, the Lumbermill is your friend.
  - Need more Miner slots? Build a Stonemason!
  - Gatherers will collect Food for your town. Build more Windmills if you need more
    Gatherer slots!
  - Towers unlock Defender slots, and fire enormous arrows at enemies. Ouch, that's
    gotta hurt!
  - Trying to build a Fishing Hut? Make sure it's on the water's edge!
  - Farms are both a building and a resource. They unlock Farmer slots and provide
    Food. Makes sense!
  - Soldiers are so cool and strong! Build a Barracks to unlock more Soldier slots.
  - Armed with bow and arrows, Rangers attack enemies from a distance. Build more
    Bowyards to unlock more Ranger slots.
  - Build a Monastery to unlock Priest roles. Priests can heal allies. Wow, take
    me to church!
  - Unlocking the Castle will open up the Paladin role. The Paladin can attack enemies
    and heal allies. Neat!
  - You're a wizard, chat! Unlock the Wizard Tower and you can be a Wizard too!
  - Something wicked this way comes! Unlock the Necro Tower to get the Necromancer
    role.
  - Any player can use !build to place a building, but only Builders can actually
    build them.
  - Not sure which buildings are currently unlocked? Just type !buildings.
  - Most buildings become increasingly expensive as you build more buildings of that
    type. Type !info, followed by the building type, to check the cost.
  - Click on Buildings to level them up, or remove them! Chat can also do this with
    !level and !remove, followed by the building type and ID.
  - You can combine directions into a single command when moving buildings around!
    Try "!up 10 left 10".
  - Don't know what to do? Check the Town Goal in the top-right corner of the screen!
  - Who should be Ruler? When the pop-up appears, type !vote to vote for someone
    in chat.
  - Anyone in chat can be the Ruler! Every hour, a pop-up will prompt chat to keep
    the Ruler or kick them out!
  - The Ruler can control the camera! Type !cam followed by a direction and an amount,
    e.g. "!cam up 10".
  - The Ruler can buy and sell resources! Type !buy or !sell, followed by an amount,
    and the resource you want to buy or sell.
  - You can recruit NPCs using the Recruit menu at the bottom of the screen. The
    Ruler can also do this with the !recruit command, followed by the role and the
    amount.
  - Click on Recruits to change their role or dismiss them. The Ruler can do this
    with !rrole and !rdismiss, followed by the Recruit's ID.
  - How do you keep track of all these pets? Type !pets to get a list of the pets
    that you own.
  - Twitch subscribers get a free Red Panda pet! Type "!pet redpanda" to switch to
    it.
  - When Fish God arrives, type !praise to praise the Fish God! You might be granted
    a special Fish God pet.
  - Switch to the Gatherer role, and you might just find a Giraffe hiding in a bush!
  - What's a Red Panda, you ask? It's kinda like a fox.
  - Buildings can be levelled up. This increases their health points and unlocks
    more role slots, but costs resources.
  - Hey mate, shut the gate! Players can walk through Gates, but enemies can't.
  - Marketplaces will give you passive Gold income. Everyone loves getting money
    for doing nothing!
  - Trees, ore and bushes will hold more resources the further they are from the
    Town Hall. Click on them to see how many resources are remaining.
  - Enemies will only come at night! Make sure you prepare your defenses during the
    day!
  - Uh oh! The more players and Recruits in your Town, the more enemies you'll attract
    at night!
  - What the heck is a Blargul? It's a weird purple thing that spits acid at you!
    Yuck!
  - Battering Rams will attack your buildings at night. Watch out!
  - Lose sight of your character? Type !ping and the game will point them out.
  - Need to get back to town quickly? Type !stuck and your character will teleport
    back to the Town Hall.
  - Need to check your XP but don't want to switch your role? Type !level followed
    by the role you want to check.
  - Hot damn, that grass is definitely the correct shade of green.
  - 'I heard there was a Squid God in this game? Is that true? '
  - "Only YOU can prevent Gold scams \u2013 wait, does this game have microtransactions
    ... ? Ah, never mind."
  - A game controlled entirely by Twitch chat? What could possibly go wrong!
  - "Welcome to Stream Town \u2013 don't worry, you'll get used to the smell."
  - Now arriving at Stream Town. Word of advice, maybe don't drink the water.
  _buildingManagerProgress: {fileID: 6230966915365309038}
